    "message": "Let the row kernels alone judge the namespaces Rust owns at the end of a tick\n\nRetire the Rust checks that walked the trees of psychological_distress_v1 and\ninformation_spread_v1 in front of their Python rules: psychological_agents_valid,\ninformation_contacts_valid and unit_values_valid. A row kernel stands in front of those rules\nnow, and on anything else the rules read the tree themselves.\n\nA row kernel's yes used to pass for a world that no longer holds what the row follows. Storing\npast NamespaceTable or IdMap, or in the world's __dict__, left a row nothing writes. rust_validated\nnow asks whether the world holds the row's tree and the maps the rows follow, so those writes reach\nthe Python rules and their errors.\n\nAdd a test for each way of writing, and a shadow of the per-tick check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
