    "tree": {
      "sha": "186085dc5136c7ac90e6a5f46ad3436f5bfddd4a",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jphacks/tkb_2615/git/trees/186085dc5136c7ac90e6a5f46ad3436f5bfddd4a"
    },
    "message": "Save the namespace or entity map a world really holds, not an old row\n\nA world whose model_state was stored in its __dict__, or a namespace or an entity written past\nNamespaceTable or IdMap, is valid, so nothing stopped the save, and capture wrote the bytes of a row\nnothing follows any more. The state was lost silently. Capture now asks the same as rust_validated\nand encodes the Python objects when the rows are not what the world holds.\n\nA write to an entity's __dict__ still does not reach a save; a test pins that and the lane doc says\nwhy it stays. The doc also records the decision on writes past a tracked dict, and that movement_v1\nnow has a row.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
